Just because this thread was sitting around begging to have an article
hung from it...

I've noticed that, with the appearance of lots of canned goods, that
the chances of finding explicitly a tin of spinach in the first half
dozen levels seems to have dropped drastically, so that my characters
not only start out 98 pound weaklings, but stay that way much, much
longer.  In fact, I think I've only seen a single can of spinach since
I started playing 3.0i Rev. 8.

Was this an intended change in game balance?  I know there are lots of
ways to improve strength that didn't exist before, but they all seem
to be available a lot more flights of stairs away from where carrying
stuff becomes a chore.

And the recent list of completely counterintuitive comparitive weights
makes me, too, want a "what does this sucker heft at" command and a
"how burdened am I" feeling as part of the game.

Totally sideways to the above, has Rev. 9 fixed the score table so that
it pages, rather than blasting by, if more than a screenful is displayed?
It's really nice to have a pager in the inventory function, how about one
for the scores if it hasn't been done.

As you might guess from my notes above, out here in leaf-land, ftp is
impossible, the ftp-by-mail process looks too painful to contemplate,
with a separate go around for each directory explored, and the nice
person who offered a mail server for patchlevel 9 also asked that it
not be overwhelmed.  Since patchlevel 8 is working for me, and compiling
patchlevel nine without a hard drive would probably take 24 solid hours
of work managing my 6 meg ramdisk, I'm getting along with level 8 for the
Amiga for now.  I was hoping for a post of the binaries, but I guess after
the "end all" level 8 turned out not to be, the various binary group
moderators are not feeling that friendly again so soon.

And c.j. silverio, a tech writer of my acquaintance of no antecedants
whatsoever posts in talk.bizarre that she was just a total winner on 3.09,
as if it were no big deal.

Sob.

Five years and still trying to hack and slash my way to the endgame, with
a tourist, without Elbereth, polypile, and all the other glorious cheats.
I have taken to #praying a bit, though; seeking the moral low ground.

